Subject: CPMS I02C Canonical Document and Golden Bundle Data Design

@ [design_uuid] 3d1cda99-3cb7-4233-befd-f99d63afd12f

& [ProposedForms] are feature gated and strict
  + CanonicalMachineSchemaDocument carries direction, root kind, type name, schema id, schema Value, root and universe fingerprints, resource account, residual ids, canonical byte length, and document digest
  + MachineSchemaBundlePayload carries profile, dialect, generator, supplied source revision, exact limits, two direction-qualified universe inventory fingerprints and accounts, and five documents keyed by root kind
  + MachineSchemaGoldenBundle carries payload, payload digest, exact-baseline fingerprint, and fixed artifact projection table
  + SchemaDocumentFormationFault reuses or extends the closed machine-schema fault vocabulary with exact path, limit, observed, and bounded message

& [PureFunctions] are bounded
  + materialize_canonical_schema_document(universe, root_kind)
  + materialize_public_procedure_schema_bundle(universes)
  + canonical_machine_schema_artifacts(bundle) returns a sorted in-memory path-to-byte map without filesystem access
  + verify_exact_schema_bundle_replay(expected_baseline, candidate) returns identical or typed mismatch, never compatible

& [DocumentAlgorithm] is ordered
  + select one root and verify its declared direction and stable schema id
  + copy normalized root object and reject preexisting $id or $defs
  + require absent or exact $schema, then set exact dialect and $id
  + select every and only named closure definition from the same universe and insert as $defs
  + normalize once, measure, enforce, digest, and independently rescan local reference closure

& [DigestProfiles] avoid self-reference
  + document digest is SHA-256 of exact canonical schema bytes
  + document fingerprint profile binds direction, root kind, type, schema id, root fingerprint, universe fingerprint, and document digest
  + bundle payload digest profile binds exact canonical payload bytes before digest fields exist
  + exact-baseline profile binds payload digest and ordered document fingerprints and digests

& [ImplementationSurfaceCandidate] remains unactivated
  + modify schema_generation.rs visibility only where canonical writer and measurement reuse requires it
  + modify lib.rs and add schema_documents.rs plus machine_schema_documents.rs tests
  + add six checked-in golden JSON artifacts generated from the signed prerequisite source revision
  + no Cargo, core, CLI, MCP, service, ecosystem, Windows, runtime, provider, or hardware source change
